  "contract": "metering-boundary",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "title": "Metering/budget field map (fleet <-> peer export)",
  "description": "The boundary map for the one frozen metering/budget record shape (issue #425). Every canonical field of metering-record.schema.json has exactly one row naming the fleet column it comes from (telemetry/metering / the budget rail) and the peer export column it must map to. A field that exists on one side only is NAMED in 'one_sided', never silently dropped; the parity gate refuses a canonical field with no row (an unmapped field). 'peer_field' is the contract name the direction issue on kushin77/deepseek asks the peer export to emit \u2014 it is a request, not a claim about their current code.",
  "sides": {
    "fleet": "telemetry/metering/, telemetry/budgets/, gateway/finops/, integrations/paperclip/budget.py",
    "peer": "kushin77/deepseek export (kushin77/deepseek#55/#71/#30); kushin77/ollama#199 is the third producer"
  },
